## Task 3: Connection Interfaces, Advantages and Disadvantages

| Connection Interface | Advantage | Disadvantage |
|---|---|---|
| USB | Provides a reliable connection and good data-transfer speed | Requires a physical cable |
| Wi-Fi | Allows wireless connections and sharing between devices on a network | May be affected by weak signals or network problems |
| Bluetooth | Provides a convenient wireless connection without a cable | Has a limited range and may be slower than USB |

Conclusion:

USB is useful for direct wired connections, Wi-Fi is convenient for network sharing, and Bluetooth is useful for short-range wireless connections.

